      "content": "#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdint>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    std::ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    std::cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, s;\n    if (!(std::cin >> n >> s)) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const std::size_t width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    const std::size_t window_size = static_cast<std::size_t>(s);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(width * width);\n    for (std::size_t row = 0; row < width; ++row) {\n        const std::size_t offset = row * width;\n        for (std::size_t col = 0; col < width; ++col) {\n            std::cin >> matrix[offset + col];\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::vector<std::int64_t> column_sums(width, 0);\n    for (std::size_t row = 0; row < window_size; ++row) {\n        const int* row_data = matrix.data() + row * width;\n        for (std::size_t col = 0; col < width; ++col) {\n            column_sums[col] += row_data[col];\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::int64_t window_sum = 0;\n    for (std::size_t col = 0; col < window_size; ++col) {\n        window_sum += column_sums[col];\n    }\n    std::int64_t best = window_sum;\n\n    for (std::size_t top = 1; top + window_size <= width; ++top) {\n        const int* outgoing = matrix.data() + (top - 1) * width;\n        const int* incoming = matrix.data() + (top + window_size - 1) * width;\n        window_sum = 0;\n        for (std::size_t col = 0; col < width; ++col) {\n            column_sums[col] += static_cast<std::int64_t>(incoming[col]) - outgoing[col];\n            window_sum += column_sums[col];\n            if (col >= window_size) {\n                window_sum -= column_sums[col - window_size];\n            }\n            if (col + 1 >= window_size && window_sum > best) {\n                best = window_sum;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::cout << best << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "A single flat row-major matrix and a contiguous sweep over column sums should improve locality while finding the maximum in O(N²) work. The full matrix is retained, trading O(N²) storage for simple sequential row access and O(N) accumulator storage.",
